  "label": "child is the one who won't be let use the oven with friends",
  "description": "The text 'mom won't let me use the oven with my friends' is mapped onto the visual entity 'child', who is depicted smiling while playing with a toy kitchen set. The child's joyful expression and engagement with the toy kitchen visually represent the child's desire to use the oven (as implied by the text) with friends, even though it is a toy. The mapping is established by the juxtaposition of the text with the child's image, where the child is the subject of the text ('me').",
